WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.360
From Post to Market,

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.540
click Listing

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.920
Updates in the left sidebar.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.180
Here are real

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.790
price changes and vehicles

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:07.810
that are no longer

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.050
in the connected inventory.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.100
Start with a price card.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.440
Compare the old price

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.520
with the new one.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.970
On a sold card,

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.040
check the vehicle

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.310
and the action shown.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.230
Choose individual vehicles

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.770
using their selection boxes.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.460
Or, if you want

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.880
to handle every change shown,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.120
use Select

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.240
All at the bottom.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.180
Check the selected count.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.440
Then click Process Updates.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.470
The Queue

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.910
shows the work in progress.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.210
In this example, AutoLander

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.970
is marking one vehicle sold.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.060
Watch for Done

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.080
on that row.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.100
That confirms

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.120
the action finished.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.500
After a price

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.020
update finishes successfully,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.380
the matching Facebook

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.000
listing shows the new price.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.040
If a row says Failed,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.060
read its message

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.100
before trying again.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:52.780
Using Auto-Pilot?

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.020
It handles price

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.110
and sold updates

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.350
for you while it's running.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.370
You don't have

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.400
to keep this page open

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.820
or watch each update.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.650
If you're posting manually,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.670
check Listing Updates as part

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.690
of your daily routine.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.270
Now find one price change,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.650
one sold card

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.070
and the selection controls.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.430
If your page

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.710
has no changes today,

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.150
there's nothing to process.
